Skip the RG353 panel detection, whose result nothing consumes.

board_late_init costs 235 ms on the RG353PS and it is all
rgxx3_detect_display(): the VO power domain, the panel reset release, the DSI
host probe, the DSI attach and a DCS read of the panel ID. None of that is used
for output - U-Boot hands over a black screen by design (0007) - and the ID's
only consumer would be a boot script patching the DT with ${panel}, which this
platform does not have: extlinux.conf and the kernel command line never mention
it.

Keep the power domain write (mainline A-TF leaves the VO domain to us; 0001)
and stop there. The kernel probes and initialises the panel itself.

Measured on the device: stopping after the DSI attach, which skips only the DCS
read, changed nothing at all (1.891 s before Linux, main_loop still at 354 ms),
so the cost is the bring-up rather than the read.

Note for later: this does not change which panels work. The shipped DTB names
anbernic,rg353p-panel, so a unit with the other panel (0x3821) is unsupported
today and was before. Supporting both means using the ID - e.g. patching the DT
in ft_board_setup() - and that would have to pay this cost again.

diff --git a/boot/Kconfig b/boot/Kconfig
--- a/boot/Kconfig
+++ b/boot/Kconfig
@@ -1309,6 +1309,16 @@
 
 	  Diagnostic builds only: this costs a timer read per initcall and
 	  needs CONFIG_BOOTSTAGE_RECORD_COUNT raised to fit the sequence.
+
+config RGXX3_SKIP_PANEL_ID
+	bool "Skip the RG353 panel detection in board_late_init"
+	help
+	  The Anbernic 353 series shipped two panels and U-Boot reads the panel
+	  ID over DSI to tell them apart, then puts the matching compatible in
+	  the environment for the boot script to patch the device tree with.
+	  Without that script the value is unused and the read costs ~200 ms.
+	  Keeps the VO power domain, the reset release and the DSI attach, so
+	  the panel is still initialised for scan-out.
 
 config BOOTSTAGE_STASH
 	bool "Stash the boot timing information in memory before booting OS"
diff --git a/board/anbernic/rgxx3_rk3566/rgxx3-rk3566.c b/board/anbernic/rgxx3_rk3566/rgxx3-rk3566.c
--- a/board/anbernic/rgxx3_rk3566/rgxx3-rk3566.c
+++ b/board/anbernic/rgxx3_rk3566/rgxx3-rk3566.c
@@ -324,6 +324,17 @@
 	 */
 	wmb();
 
+	if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_RGXX3_SKIP_PANEL_ID)) {
+		/*
+		 * The panel ID only picks a compatible string for a boot script to
+		 * patch the DT with, and this platform has no such script, so all of
+		 * this is dead weight: the DSI bring-up alone is ~235 ms of
+		 * board_late_init. Keep the power domain write above - mainline A-TF
+		 * does not do it - and leave the panel initialisation to the kernel.
+		 */
+		return 0;
+	}
+
 	/*
 	 * Take panel out of reset status.
 	 * Set GPIO4_A0 to output.
